Package: displaceR
Title: Run the DISPLACE Fisheries Simulator from R
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    person("Pol", "Carbo Mestre", email = "polcarbo@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: A thin R interface to the DISPLACE individual-based fisheries
    simulator. The package contains no compiled code: it downloads a prebuilt
    headless Linux binary published by the companion build pipeline, writes and
    validates DISPLACE input files, runs the simulator, and reads its SQLite and
    text outputs back into data frames. Modelled on the r4ss / cmdstanr pattern
    where the backend is installed separately into a user directory.
License: GPL-2
URL: https://github.com/pcarbomestre/displaceR
BugReports: https://github.com/pcarbomestre/displaceR/issues
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends:
    R (>= 4.0)
Imports:
    tools,
    utils
Suggests:
    DBI,
    RSQLite,
    digest,
    jsonlite,
    testthat (>= 3.0.0)
Config/testthat/edition: 3
RoxygenNote: 7.3.1
SystemRequirements: A 64-bit Linux host. The DISPLACE simulator binary is
    downloaded at runtime by install_displace(); no compiler or CMake is
    required on the target machine.
